ercontent.com/u/59910575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla","html_url":"https://github.com/OzelotVanilla","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OzelotVanilla/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-08T07:21:36Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T07:21:36Z","body":"> What's the point of using upstream clang instead of Apple-clang in a first place? Installing and using Homebrew require installing Xcode command line tools, so you already have Apple-clang installed anyway.\r\n\r\n(Some copied from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107199#issuecomment-2953608645)\r\n\r\nSince it is off-topic, so I would say for personal use.\r\nHowever, from the [documentation page](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/compiling/compiling_for_macos.html), no requirements for compiler (type or version) is written in the requirement, so for me I believe somehow that, the latest version of compiler is considered acceptable when compiling. At least works for Vulkan I installed from `brew`, it looks fine.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2953666469/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":nul